{
    "background_story": "Kali was a spirited and adventurous young girl who lived in a small coastal town. She spent most of her days exploring the rugged shoreline and dreaming of far-off lands. One day, while wandering through the town's historic district, Kali stumbled upon an old, rusty flagpole standing tall in the town square. As she gazed up at the pole, she felt an inexplicable connection to it. She began to visit the flagpole every day, watching as the wind whipped the flags into a frenzy. Kali's fascination with the flagpole inspired her to learn about the town's rich maritime history. She spent hours poring over old books and talking to locals, eventually becoming the town's youngest and most knowledgeable historian. The flagpole became a symbol of Kali's curiosity and love for her community's heritage.",
